+# Synthetic Playwright Identities — Contract
+
+## Overview
+
+Idempotent provisioning contract for three synthetic Audiobookshelf identities
+used by Playwright E2E tests. The provisioning script creates/manages Keycloak
+users without exposing credentials.
+
+## Identities
+
+| Username | Role | Group | Purpose |
+|----------|------|-------|---------|
+| `pw-e2e-abs-user` | E2E user | `audiobookshelf-users` | Standard user flows |
+| `pw-e2e-abs-admin` | E2E admin | `audiobookshelf-admins` | Admin role coverage |
+| `pw-e2e-abs-denied` | E2E denied | (none) | Authorization negative tests |
+
+## Naming Convention
+
+- Username: `pw-e2e-<service>-<role>` (PWR-020 compliant)
+- Display name: same as username (visible automation marker)
+- Email: `pw-e2e-<service>-<role>@homelab.test` (no real data)
+- No personal data (PWR-021 compliant)
+
+## Provisioning Script
+
+**Path:** `pi/audiobookshelf/scripts/setup-playwright-identities.sh`
+
+### Modes
+
+| Mode | Flag | Behavior |
+|------|------|----------|
+| Dry-run | `--dry-run` (default) | Mock kcadm calls, prove realm/groups exist |
+| Commit | `--commit` | Execute real provisioning (operator runtime only) |
+
+### Security Constraints
+
+- Refuses `set -x` (xtrace) to prevent secret leakage
+- Never accepts secrets via command-line arguments
+- Never prints existing passwords or client credentials
+- Requires `KCADM` env var pointing to a kcadm binary or mock
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Required | Description |
+|----------|----------|-------------|
+| `KCADM` | Yes | Path to kcadm binary or mock |
+| `DRY_RUN` | No | Override dry-run mode (`true`/`false`) |
+
+## Test Coverage
+
+**Path:** `pi/tests/test_playwright_identities.sh`
+
+13 mock tests covering:
+- xtrace refusal
+- dry-run and commit modes
+- Help flag and argument validation
+- Realm/group/client assertions
+- Idempotent execution
+- Secret-free output
+- Identity provisioning order
+
+Run: `bash pi/tests/test_playwright_identities.sh`
+
+## Runtime Injection
+
+Credentials are injected at container start via environment variables:
+- `PW_E2E_ABS_USER` — username
+- `PW_E2E_ABS_PASSWORD` — password
+
+The provisioning script generates and stores passwords in Keycloak; the test
+runner receives them at runtime. Passwords are never committed to code.
